From 5f72493a2552d42ba48b58c4075cad0ed4e76f76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: schoeremy <jeremyfroeb2007@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:14:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 57/59] nxhost: ntc, error contexts and built-in CA
 certificates for Splatoon 3 online

Signed in to Nextendo, Splatoon 3 now goes online at boot and hit three
more services that answered success without what the SDK expects:

- ntc cmd 0 (OpenEnsureNetworkClockAvailabilityService) returned no object;
  nn::time::AsyncEnsureNetworkClockAvailabilityTask dereferenced null. It now
  gets a service whose check finishes at once (time:u's network clock already
  follows the host clock).
- ssl:s GetCertificateBufSize/GetCertificates (cmds 3/2) returned nothing.
  The game runs its own BoringSSL and loads the console's root CAs through
  them, so it gave up before connecting. ssl/ssl:s now serve the entries of
  the firmware's ssl_TrustedCerts.bdf (0100000000000800; "sslT", count,
  16-byte entries with offsets from the end of the header): 127 certs, the
  game asks for ids 1, 2, 0x3e8, 0x3f3-0x3f5, 0x409. ssl:s is routed to the
  ssl service in Nextendo mode.
- ectx:aw cmd 0 (CreateContextRegistrar) returned no object; nn::err crashed
  filing an error. It now gets a registrar that logs the result code.

In a sandbox without outbound network the game now resolves the NPLN tenant,
connects to 51.178.29.194:443, gets refused and reports 2321-4992 instead
of crashing.
